-      "id": "US-890",
-      "title": "Migrate messaging-limits tier model to 100K flat cap (Q2 2026)",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Meta is removing the 2K and 10K daily messaging limit tiers in Q2 2026; any verified business immediately receives 100K/day. The existing messaging-limits.ts still models tiers '250', '2000', '10000', '100000'. The admin tier selector and in-app messaging-limit display must be updated to reflect the new flat-cap model and remove obsolete lower tiers.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "TIER_LIMITS constant in messaging-limits.ts removes '250' and '2000' tiers",
-        "PUT /analytics/messaging-limits/tier returns 400 if tier '250' or '2000' is supplied",
-        "Admin UI tier dropdown shows only '10000', '100000', and 'unlimited' as selectable options",
-        "Existing rows in app_settings table with value '250' or '2000' are auto-migrated to '10000' on startup",
-        "Vitest unit test asserts 200 response for valid tiers and 400 for removed tiers"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Source: Meta developer docs — https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/whatsapp/upcoming-messaging-limits-changes/",
-        "Migration must be backward-compatible; if DB row is missing, default to '100000' not '250'",
-        "Admin notification should be sent once when auto-migration executes"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
