-      "id": "US-891",
-      "title": "WhatsApp portfolio pacing monitor: detect and alert when batch delivery is paused",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Meta's portfolio pacing silently pauses bulk template sends mid-campaign when quality signals (blocks, complaints) are negative. There is currently no mechanism in Rainbow AI to detect that a scheduled send was paused or that quality feedback triggered a hold, meaning operators discover delivery failures only after the fact.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "GET /analytics/messaging-limits returns a pacingPaused: boolean field derived from Meta Graph API quality signals",
-        "When pacingPaused is true, admin dashboard displays a visible warning banner",
-        "Admin notification is sent within 5 minutes of a pacing pause being detected",
-        "Alert body includes the affected template name and percentage of batch not yet delivered",
-        "Vitest test mocks the Meta quality signal endpoint and asserts the correct pacingPaused state is surfaced"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Poll Meta's WABA health/quality endpoint: GET /{phone-number-id}/quality_rating",
-        "Store last known pacing state in app_settings to avoid repeated notifications",
-        "Reference: https://www.fyno.io/blog/how-does-whatsapp-template-pacing-work-a-detailed-guide-cm2tykayw00d7wixo00hhiuxk"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [
