-    {
-      "id": "US-892",
-      "title": "WABA webhook subscription health check on server startup",
-      "priority": "high",
-      "description": "Meta's developer experience change in late 2025 means the WABA-to-App webhook subscription can fail silently: the webhook URL is verified but the app never actually receives events. Rainbow AI has no startup check that confirms the WABA subscription is active, so a silently broken subscription could cause all inbound WhatsApp messages to go missing without any alert.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "On server startup, a check calls GET /{waba-id}/subscribed_apps and confirms the app is subscribed",
-        "If the subscription is missing, the check automatically resubscribes via POST /{waba-id}/subscribed_apps",
-        "Admin notification is sent if auto-resubscription fails",
-        "Health endpoint GET /health returns webhookSubscribed: true|false",
-        "The check is skipped gracefully when WABA credentials are absent (e.g., development environment)",
-        "Vitest test mocks the Meta Graph API and asserts resubscription is attempted when subscription is absent"
-      ],
-      "technicalNotes": [
-        "Use the existing Meta Graph API token stored in env vars",
-        "Reference: https://hookdeck.com/webhooks/platforms/guide-to-whatsapp-webhooks-features-and-best-practices",
-        "Subscription check should run once on startup and then every 6 hours via setInterval"
-      ],
-      "dependencies": [],
-      "estimatedComplexity": "medium",
-      "passes": false,
-      "filesTouch": [
