-    {
-      "id": "US-895",
-      "title": "Persist raw webhook payloads to durable storage before processing",
-      "priority": "medium",
-      "description": "Best practice for WhatsApp Cloud API webhook reliability requires logging every raw payload to durable storage before any processing so that lost or failed events can be replayed. Currently, Rainbow AI processes messages directly in-memory after BullMQ dequeues them; if processing fails mid-flight and the DLQ entry lacks the original raw payload, the message is unrecoverable.",
-      "acceptanceCriteria": [
-        "Every inbound webhook payload is written to a webhook_raw_events table (or S3 object) before the BullMQ job is enqueued",
-        "Each raw event row includes: event_id UUID, received_at timestamp, profile, payload JSONB, processed BOOLEAN",
-        "The DLQ entry references the raw event ID so operators can replay the original payload",
-        "GET /admin/dlq/:jobId returns the associated raw event payload",
-        "Vitest test asserts raw event is persisted even when downstream processing throws"
-      ],
